# memory_gap_ram_holes: Guest RAM in five ranges with a hole between the first and the rest. A depth-2 task whose task root and first-level table are in R1 and whose second-level table is in R4 (the page-table walk reads each through the range that holds it); a buffer of four pages physically contiguous across R1, R2 and R3 (the memory map maps it in three pieces), one in R4, and one whose page is in the hole. In the map and isolate setups the fill across the ranges lands in all four pages; in the blocks setup the page-table walk coalesces the four pages into one physical range, which the host (as QEMU's) cannot map across its ranges, so the command faults. The page in the hole faults in every setup: no range holds it ("Incomplete range" in-process; the host's map_memory fails in blocks).
